{
  "$comment": [
    "Economic calendar source. Two kinds of entries:",
    "",
    "  recurring — statistical releases that follow a published, stable schedule",
    "              (e.g. US nonfarm payrolls is always the first Friday). These",
    "              are expanded for any month, so this file never goes stale.",
    "              They are surfaced in the UI as 추정 (estimated) because the",
    "              agency can shift a release by a day.",
    "",
    "  anchors   — one-off dates that cannot be derived from a rule: central-bank",
    "              meetings, ad-hoc briefings. Add them here as they are published",
    "              (FOMC and 한은 금통위 publish a full-year schedule in advance).",
    "              These render as 확정 (confirmed). Past anchors are ignored, so",
    "              leaving old ones here is harmless.",
    "",
    "Times are LOCAL to the release agency and converted to KST for display,",
    "so US releases follow EST/EDT automatically instead of drifting an hour."
  ],

